From 705b9978430a93395e9ae9e2f8cd240fc0b8289f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:48:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 065/125] tools decode-link: fixes from the review

What Xray accepts and sing-box refuses is now settled when the link is read,
not when the outbound starts: fingerprints (any case, Chrome's by default,
"unsafe" for none, unknown ones refused), flows (the udp443 form of Vision
read as Vision, others refused, any flow over xhttp refused), a gRPC service
name that is a custom path, and everything the xhttp transport checks in its
options. The stream-one check is on the link's mode, where Xray has it.

Also: every unreadable link is reported, by its position or its line, in
plain lines; error messages do not repeat parts of the link; two links on a
line are refused; what extra names is settled by extra, also as false; the
host among several Host headers no longer depends on map order; the download
leg takes no upload settings; splithttpSettings beside a null xhttpSettings,
upper case in security and network, brackets around an address.
